use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component Radio:
    description:
        A radio is one option in a set where only one can be picked. It is
        either picked or not, has a label, and can't be un-picked by clicking
        it again; picking another option is the only way to change it.

    group:
        A radio always belongs to a RadioGroup, which decides which radio is
        picked. A radio on its own has no meaning. Each radio has its own
        value, which is what the group holds when that radio is picked.

    label:
        A radio has a name, usually shown as a label next to it. Clicking the
        label works the same as clicking the radio.

    disabled:
        A disabled radio can't be picked, and it's clear to the user that it's
        unavailable. If it was already picked, it stays picked.
